      <itunes:episode>412</itunes:episode>
      <description><![CDATA[<p>Overbooking looks like a scandal every time someone gets bumped. Inside the airline, it is a math problem. Reporters Priya Nair and Tom Okafor explain how carriers decide how many extra tickets to sell, why the practice survives, and what happens when the bet goes wrong.</p><p>Read more: <a href="https://www.example.com/overbooking">example.com/overbooking</a></p>]]></description>
